What is the value of `j` at the end of execution of the following C program?

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int incr(int i) {
    static int count = 0;
    count = count + i;
    return count;
}
int main() {
    int i, j;
    for (i = 0; i <= 4; i++)
        j = incr(i);
    return 0;
}
```

Consider the recursive C function:

```c
int f(int n) {
